WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:09.478
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.778 --> 00:00:14.497
Unit five: Writing Emails. Today you will write a clear and polite email.

4
00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:17.600
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:21.789
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.872
Subject line.

7
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:27.591
Subject line means the short title of an email.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.904
Write a clear subject line.

9
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:33.006
Your turn. Say: Subject line.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:37.204
Subject line.

11
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.649
Greeting.

12
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.963
Greeting means the opening words of a message.

13
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.760
Start with a greeting.

14
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.654
Your turn. Say: Greeting.

15
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.257
Greeting.

16
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.029
Attach.

17
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:55.573
Attach means to add a file to an email.

18
00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:57.777
I attach my report.

19
00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:01.036
Your turn. Say: Attach.

20
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.971
Attach.

21
00:01:05.717 --> 00:01:06.915
Request.

22
00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:10.543
Request means asking for something politely.

23
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.894
I have a request for you.

24
00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:16.182
Your turn. Say: Request.

25
00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.301
Request.

26
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.098
Regards.

27
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.733
Regards means a polite way to end a message.

28
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:27.736
Best regards, Sokha.

29
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.851
Your turn. Say: Regards.

30
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.840
Regards.

31
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:36.422
Polite.

32
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:39.532
Polite means showing good manners.

33
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:41.652
Be polite in your email.

34
00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.542
Your turn. Say: Polite.

35
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.239
Polite.

36
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:49.926
Reply.

37
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.090
Reply means to answer a message.

38
00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:55.242
Please reply by Friday.

39
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.491
Your turn. Say: Reply.

40
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.427
Reply.

41
00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:03.941
Brief.

42
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.648
Brief means short and clear.

43
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.878
Keep your email brief.

44
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:11.857
Your turn. Say: Brief.

45
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.457
Brief.

46
00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:20.115
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.170
Visal, how do I write a good email?

48
00:02:24.283 --> 00:02:32.903
Start with a clear subject line and a greeting like Dear Ms Chan. State your purpose in the first sentence, then give details.

49
00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:34.948
How do I end it?

50
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:43.648
Say thank you, then close with Best regards and your name. If you attach a file, mention it in the email.

51
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.297
How polite should I be?

52
00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:55.135
Use please and could you in a request. For example, could you send me the schedule? Keep the email brief and clear.

53
00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.172
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.017 --> 00:03:01.620
Grammar focus: Polite requests.

55
00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.060
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.761
Could you send me the schedule, please?

57
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.742
Could you reply by Friday, please?

58
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:15.301
Use could you plus the base verb to make a polite request. Add please and say thank you at the end.

59
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.422
Be careful! Don't say: Could you to send me it?

60
00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.122
Say: Could you send it to me?

61
00:03:23.422 --> 00:03:24.807
No to after could you.

62
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.485
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.916
An Email to a Teacher.

64
00:03:31.216 --> 00:03:33.274
Dara writes an email to his teacher.

65
00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.835
His subject line says Question about homework.

66
00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.773
He starts with Dear Mr Lee and states his purpose.

67
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:44.637
He asks politely, Could you explain question three?

68
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:47.958
He ends with Best regards and his name.

69
00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:53.277
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:56.418
The subject line is the email's blank.

71
00:03:56.718 --> 00:04:00.058
A, end. B, stamp. C, title.

72
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.425
The answer is C: title.

73
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:08.188
Dear Mr Lee is a blank.

74
00:04:08.488 --> 00:04:12.060
A, greeting. B, reply. C, file.

75
00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.263
The answer is A: greeting.

76
00:04:18.417 --> 00:04:20.149
Could you is a blank request.

77
00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:23.650
A, loud. B, polite. C, rude.

78
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.107
The answer is B: polite.

79
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.122
Best regards is a polite blank.

80
00:04:32.422 --> 00:04:35.762
A, title. B, topic. C, ending.

81
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.323
The answer is C: ending.

82
00:04:42.483 --> 00:04:44.390
Dara keeps his email blank.

83
00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.798
A, brief. B, secret. C, wet.

84
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:52.961
The answer is A: brief.

85
00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:57.550
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:04:58.417 --> 00:05:00.126
How do you write a polite email?

87
00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:10.487
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:10.787 --> 00:05:20.617
I write a clear subject line and start with a greeting. I state my purpose, use could you and please, and say thank you. I end with Best regards and my name.

89
00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:22.672
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:27.710
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and polite requests.

91
00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.580
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

92
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.428
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:05:34.728 --> 00:05:37.879
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

